OUTPUT PATH RECONCILIATION (no silent drift — covenant #9)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
The generated prompt names the output dir `apps/apple/TeslaSync/Features/Automations/**`.
That path does NOT exist in this repo and is NOT a project.yml source group. The repo's
real, compiled canonical page home is `apps/apple/Sources/Features/<Domain>/` — proven by the
DONE sibling pages (ApiPlaygroundPage, DiskForecastPage, … all under Sources/Features/Admin).
`Sources` is a project.yml source path (createIntermediateGroups), shared by the iOS + macOS
app targets (ADR-002). The page therefore ships at `apps/apple/Sources/Features/Automations/**`
— the faithful equivalent of the prompt's `Features/Automations`. Strings ship in the platform
catalog `apps/apple/Localization/Localizable.xcstrings` (an allowed file). This mapping is the
only deviation from the literal prompt path and is recorded here per covenant #9.

NAVIGATION (the unit is (unrouted)):
The web `AutomationActivityFeed` is a SECTION the `/automations` page (`AutomationsList`, which
owns the `.automations` AppRoute) renders inline — NOT a standalone route. So this unit does NOT
take a top-level `AppRoute` (that would hijack AutomationsList's route). Instead it ships a typed
`NavigationDestination` seam — `AutomationActivityFeedLink` + `View.automationActivityFeedDestination()`
+ `AutomationActivityFeedRouteRegistration.make(...)` — that any `NavigationStack` (the future
AutomationsList route) adopts to deep-link the full-screen feed. No edits to the P4 shell
(AppShell/AppRoute/TeslaSyncApp) were made — correct for an unrouted unit and consistent with the
predecessor-bypass rule (covenant #7).

